.TH PASSAGE 1 "June 2026" "passage" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
passage \- terminal UI for GNU Pass with pins, recents, and native TOTP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B passage
[\fIfilter\fR]
.br
.B passage mfa
[\fIfilter\fR]
.br
.B passage
\fIcommand\fR [\fIflags\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B passage
reads a GNU Pass password store, presents an interactive terminal picker,
copies passwords, reveals secrets only on explicit command, and generates TOTP
codes from sibling
.I mfa
entries.
.PP
GNU Pass remains the source of truth. passage stores only local metadata:
pins and last-used timestamps.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
List entries. Supports
.BR --json ,
.BR --filter ,
and
.BR --mfa .
.TP
.B show
Show metadata for one entry. Does not decrypt secrets.
.TP
.B copy
Copy an entry's password, defined as the first line of
.BR "pass show" .
.TP
.B reveal
Reveal an entry's password until a key is pressed. Also attempts to copy it.
.TP
.B totp
Generate a TOTP code from
.I ENTRY/mfa
or from
.I ENTRY
itself when it ends in
.IR /mfa .
.TP
.B mfa
Open the picker in MFA-only mode.
.TP
.B pin / unpin
Set or clear an entry pin.
.TP
.B clear-recents / clear-pins / clear-clipboard
Clear local metadata or clipboard contents.
.TP
.B insert
Create or overwrite an entry, reading the secret from stdin (the first line, or
the whole stream with
.BR --multiline ).
Refuses early if the target folder is read-only.
.TP
.B generate
Generate a random password for a new entry and copy it to the clipboard
(unless
.BR --no-copy ).
Accepts an optional length and
.BR --no-symbols .
Refuses early if the target folder is read-only.
.TP
.B edit
Open an entry in $EDITOR via pass and re-encrypt it. Refuses early if the
folder is read-only.
.TP
.B rm
Remove an entry, or a subtree with
.BR --recursive .
Prompts for confirmation unless
.BR --yes .
.TP
.B doctor
Check pass, gpg, clipboard tools, and .gpg-id recipient health.
.TP
.B access
Report, per .gpg-id scope, whether you can encrypt to all recipients
.RB ( writable ),
can only decrypt
.RB ( "read-only" ),
or neither
.RB ( "no access" ).
Writability is decided by a real probe-encrypt, not by ownertrust. With an
optional
.I ENTRY
argument, reports only the scope governing it. Exits 2 when any reported scope
is not writable.
.TP
.B trust
Make a read-only scope writable by local-signing the recipients gpg cannot yet
encrypt to.
.I SCOPE
is an entry path or folder; its nearest .gpg-id governs. Default strength is
local-sign only;
.B --full
also raises ownertrust to full (5), never downgrading existing 5/6.
.B --import-dir
.I DIR
imports and trusts every public-key file in
.IR DIR .
.B --yes
applies without the confirmation prompt;
.B --json
prints the dry-run plan only and never mutates the keyring.
.TP
.B keys
List local GPG public keys, ownertrust, and secret-key availability.
.TP
.B version
Print build version information.
.SH TUI KEYS
.PP
Lowercase printable characters always type into the fuzzy filter. The write and
trust actions are bound to the shifted (uppercase) letters; because matching is
case-insensitive you never need uppercase to filter, so you can narrow with a
lowercase filter and then act with a shifted key. Read-only folders show an
.B RO
badge (or
.B NO
for no-access).
.TP
.B Enter
Run the default action: copy password, or show/copy TOTP on an MFA-secret row.
.TP
.B N
New entry: enter a path (TAB completes folders shell-style, with a live list of
the current folder's existing entries; shift+TAB goes up a level), then type a
secret (entered twice to confirm; ^R shows/hides the characters) or generate one.
.TP
.B G
Generate a new entry.
.TP
.B E
Edit the selected entry in $EDITOR.
.TP
.B D
Delete the selected entry (with confirmation).
.TP
.B T
Trust the selected entry's folder — local-sign recipients to make it writable.
.TP
.B I
Import keys: browse to a folder of public-key files and import + local-sign them
all (gpgobble parity).
.TP
.B S
Import secret key(s): browse to a folder or a single key file and import your
secret key(s), setting them to ultimate ownertrust (the fix for a new machine,
where gpg does not auto-trust imported keys). Public-only keys are imported but
left untrusted.
.TP
.B Ctrl-Y
Copy password; in MFA-only mode, show/copy TOTP.
.TP
.B Ctrl-R
Reveal password; in MFA-only mode, show/copy TOTP.
.TP
.B Ctrl-T
Show/copy TOTP, or reveal the stored secret on an MFA-secret row.
.TP
.B P
Toggle pin (a shifted command, like N/G/E/D/T/I/S; lowercase still filters).
.TP
.B Ctrl-P / Ctrl-N
Move the cursor up / down (also Up/Down arrows).
.TP
.B Ctrl-F
Toggle MFA-only mode.
.TP
.B Ctrl-O
Open the interactive theme editor.
.TP
.B Ctrl-X
Clear clipboard.
.TP
.B Ctrl-U
Unpin all entries.
.TP
.B Ctrl-E
Clear recents.
.TP
.B Ctrl-D
Open doctor.
.TP
.B Ctrl-K
Open local key list.
.TP
.B Esc / Ctrl-C / Ctrl-Q
Quit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PASSWORD_STORE_DIR
Pass store root. Defaults to
.IR ~/.password-store .
.TP
.B PASSAGE_STATE_DIR
State directory override.
.TP
.B PASSAGE_PASS_BINARY
Override the pass executable.
.TP
.B PASSAGE_THEME_FILE
Theme config file.
.TP
.B PASSAGE_NO_COLOR, NO_COLOR
Disable color.
.TP
.B PASSAGE_NO_OSC52
Disable terminal OSC 52 clipboard fallback.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.password-store
Default GNU Pass store.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/passage/state.json
Default Linux state file.
.TP
.I ~/Library/Application Support/passage/state.json
Default macOS state file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pass (1),
.BR gpg (1)
